# Git commit messages

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). English only. Imperative mood. The subject explains **why**, not which files changed.

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short summary>
```

Allowed types: `feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `perf` `test` `build` `ci` `chore` `revert`

## Rules

- Subject ≤ 72 characters, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period
- Optional body: 1–2 sentences on motivation, separated by a blank line. Omit the body if the subject is enough
- Breaking change: `feat!:` (or other type with `!`) and/or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Do not mention AI or Cursor, and do not add `Co-authored-by`, unless asked
- When the agent commits, pass the message via HEREDOC (not `-m` twice)

## Examples

```
feat(search): rank custom keywords above default aliases

fix(paste): restore the previous clipboard after inserting an emoji

docs: describe how to add personal keywords
```

```
# Bad — what, not why; not conventional
Updated files
Added Fuse.js and changed App.svelte
feat: added search and paste and also tweaked css
```
